<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louisiana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louisiana was a vast French colonial territory in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> covering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> basin, named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>. It was claimed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the late seventeenth century and was part of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French colonial empire</a>. France sold the territory to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana-purchase">Louisiana Purchase</a> of 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louisiana.jpg" alt="Louisiana" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Curtis Vann, Jr. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Louisiana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
